          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.084,
            0.743,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": "of a magnetic substance. Separation of magnetic and non-magnetic substances by using a magnet is called **magnetic separation.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.175,
            0.608,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "Nowadays, recyclers use magnets to separate iron articles from a heap of waste."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.26,
            0.199,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.214,
            0.605,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "In many industries, the waste material often contains scrap iron. This is separated from the heap of waste materials using magnets fitted to a crane."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.317,
            0.214,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "**More to know!**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.309,
            0.594,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": "The scrap iron can be recycled and reused."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.656,
            0.16,
            0.783,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.634,
                0.331,
                0.803,
                0.348
              ],
              "content": "Magnetic separation"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.385,
            0.744,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": "Malli and Valli had delightful holidays and the ‘Bharat ki Yatra’ (tour of India) filled with fun will be an ever lasting memory for them."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.447,
            0.744,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": "They not only enjoyed exploring different regions of India but also gained a lot of knowledge about various methods of separation of substances."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.52,
            0.372,
            0.543
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 9.6: Let us play"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.553,
            0.683,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "Write the following phrases on small slips of paper—"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.582,
            0.551,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "1. Separating small stones from pulses."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.607,
            0.499,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": "2. Churning curd to obtain butter."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.631,
            0.743,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "3. Taking out green chillies from cooked dalia (dish made of broken wheat) or poha (dish made of flattened rice)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.677,
            0.539,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": "4. Taking out seeds from watermelon."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.701,
            0.743,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": "5. Sorting piles of sawdust and iron nails from a mixed heap of building material."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.746,
            0.743,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "6. Picking marigold flowers from a heap of other flowers to make a garland."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.791,
            0.486,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": "7. Separating pebbles from sand."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.816,
            0.607,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": "8. Separating coconut pieces from rice flour."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.841,
            0.443,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": "9. Separating oil from water."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.866,
            0.52,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": "10. Separating salt from salt solution."
